turns.content:
ruit blossoms open toward struggle against winds strong,
Slowly transforming rigid grief while singing softly long;
Wise perseverance writes stories mental pages white—
Scars becoming constellations visible only at night.

Fingerprints remain after hands release hold,
Memories shaping us though seasons unfold;
What falls forms fertile ground anew—
Nurturing growth spring that winter held in too.

Tightening fences keep out nothing strengthens; inner vault sealed cannot bear;
True healing requires embracing pain's grave everywhere;
Strength blooms secretly beneath visible disguise worn thin—
Wonder emerging slowly through hearts that suffer and grin.

Resilience unfolds petals layer by layer unwritten first—
Not in demonstration loud obviously bruised nearly burst;
Comfort found not when no more feeling acknowledges deep despair—
But acknowledging depths before false calms inhibit real repair.

